### Page 1 of 2

```text
PUBLIC SERVICES COMMITTEE
MINUTES
Due to the President’s Day holiday, a meeting of the Public Services Committee was instead held
on Wednesday, February 21, 2024, in Committee Room 104 and via electronic meeting, starting
at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS: Scott Roybal, Chairman, Dr. Rinne, and Tom Segrave.
Absent:
Pete Layboum.
AGENDA ITEMS
16.
RESOLUTION
— Authorizing the Mayor and the City Clerk to sign a Final Plat for The
Bluffs,
12th Filing, City of Cheyenne, Laramie County, Wyoming (located East of
Converse Avenue and South of Storey Boulevard). (POSTPONED FROM FEBRUARY
12, 2024)
Mr. Segrave moved to adopt, noting Planning Commission’s condition to provide an updated
traffic study has been met and prior to the mylars being signed (a) an easement across Townsend
Place Apartments LP be recorded to allow Wild Bluff to connect into Converse Avenue and (b)
the plat map be modified to allow an added auxiliary lane and future roadway transition on the
south side of the Storey Boulevard from Converse Avenue to Ogden Road. A 10’ Right-of-way
width and! or a perpetual utility and access easement shall be provided to allow the construction
of the auxiliary lane as approved by the City Engineer, seconded by Dr. Rinne. Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and Randy Guill,
Edwards Development Company, spoke in support of the proposed conditions.
Committee
members Rinne and Segrave commented on the item.
23.
CONTRACT MODIFICATIONS:
b)
Contract Modification #1 to Contract #3920 between the City of Cheyenne and
Charles E. Bales regarding Street improvements located adjacent to 3618 Charles
Street. (POSTPONED FROM FEBRUARY 12, 2024)
Mr. Segrave moved to approve, seconded by Dr. Rinne.
Mr. Segrave moved to amend by
substitute dated February 20, 2024, seconded by Dr. Rinne.
Motion to amend carried by
unanimous voice vote. Main motion, as amended, carried by unanimous voice vote.
Tom Cobb, City Engineer, provided a staff report and Charles Bloom, Planning & Development
Department Director, provided additional information. Committee members Rinne and Segrave
commented on the item and public comment was made by Ed Bales.
```

